{"id": "section-body-09579", "title": "Management", "chapterId": "chapter-ten", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "POISONING", "Acute Alcohol Intoxication", "Management of Skin Contamination"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-09579", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Management", "runs": [{"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-09580", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Principles of management include supportive therapies.", "runs": [{"text": "Principles"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "management"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "include"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "supportive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "therapies."}]}, {"id": "body-09581", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Intravascular\tvolume\texpansion (colloids/crystalloid)", "runs": [{"text": "Intravascular"}, {"text": "\t"}, {"text": "volume"}, {"text": "\t"}, {"text": "expansion (colloids/crystalloid)"}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1489"}}, {"id": "body-09582", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Opiates analgesia usually required (follow WHO analgesic ladder)", "runs": [{"text": "Opiates analgesia usually required (follow WHO analgesic ladder)"}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1489"}}, {"id": "body-09586", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Enteral feeding, (only in absence of illeus) start within 72 hours", "runs": [{"text": "Enteral feeding, (only in absence of illeus) start within 72 hours"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1489"}}, {"id": "body-09587", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Correction of electrolytes and metabolic deficit accordingly", "runs": [{"text": "Correction"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "electrolytes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "metabolic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "deficit "}, {"text": "accordingly"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1489"}}, {"id": "body-09590", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-09591", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "B: ceftriaxone (IV) 1g 12hourly for 7days", "runs": [{"text": "B:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "ceftriaxone"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(IV)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "1g"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "12hourly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "7days"}]}, {"id": "body-09592", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-09593", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "C: ciprofloxacin (IV) 200-400mg 12hourly for 7days", "runs": [{"text": "C:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "ciprofloxacin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(IV)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "200-400mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "12hourly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "7days"}]}, {"id": "body-09594", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "AND", "runs": [{"text": "AND"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-09595", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "B: metronidazole (IV) 500mg 8hourly for 7days", "runs": [{"text": "B:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "metronidazole"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(IV)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "500mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "8hourly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "7days"}]}, {"id": "body-09596", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-09597", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "S: meropenem (IV) 1g 8hourly for 7days", "runs": [{"text": "S:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "meropenem"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(IV)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "1g"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "8hourly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "7days"}]}, {"id": "body-09598-textbox1-00001", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Normal", "text": "Note", "runs": [{"text": "Note", "bold": true}]}, {"id": "body-09598-textbox1-00002", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Fever can be because of pancreatitis itself; antibiotics should be avoided before 7 days. Pancreatic necrosis: Nonviable pancreatic tissue. CT-guided FNA if infection suspected. Sterile necrosis: if asymptomatic, can be managed expectantly, no role for prophylactic antibiotics. Infected necrosis: high mortality. Treat with carbapenem or metronidazole plus fluoroquinolone", "runs": [{"text": "Fever can be because of pancreatitis itself; antibiotics should be avoided before 7 days. "}, {"text": "Pancreatic necrosis: ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Nonviable pancreatic tissue. CT-guided FNA if infection suspected. "}, {"text": "Sterile necrosis: ", "bold": true}, {"text": "if asymptomatic, can be managed"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "expectantly,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "no"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "role"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "prophylactic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "antibiotics."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Infected", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "necrosis", "bold": true}, {"text": ":"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "high"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mortality."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Treat"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "carbapenem or metronidazole plus fluoroquinolone"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1488"}}, {"id": "body-09598-textbox1-00003", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "If stable, defer drainage to >4 weeks. If symptomatic or unstable, percutaneous drainage and minimally invasive surgical debridement or endoscopic necrosectomy superior to open necrosectomy. ERCP + Sphincterotomy may be needed.", "runs": [{"text": "If stable, defer drainage to >4 weeks. If symptomatic or unstable, percutaneous drainage and minimally invasive surgical debridement or endoscopic necrosectomy superior to open necrosectomy. ERCP + Sphincterotomy may be needed."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1488"}}], "source": {"file": "medical.docx", "chapter": "Gastrointestinal disease conditions", "start": "body-09579", "end": "body-09598-textbox1-00003"}}